Integration follow-up: the ASan-only RenderDescriptor dealloc SEGV was a test teardown double-release of the shared path_cubic functions (the new preserve descriptor released functions still owned by the earlier descriptor). Fixed by retaining those two function pointers in the preserve descriptor. Current wrapper hash 81ec9917034b0287041c1f2a2a246ac821c6df33298c3af0aa5644b06438d26e; both ASan/UBSan fake-JM binaries exit0 with full PASS:
- 128 TEGU_INERT_PIPELINE total from 130 creations; 32 TEGU_INERT_DRAW_REFUSED from 40 draws;
- path_cubic all-four active masks -> active4/main2/preserve0xb, command count2, status4;
- TEGU_INERT_PIPELINE path_blit v=path_blit_vert_lpf f=path_blit_frag_lpf fmt=80,80,10 reason=true-MRT framebuffer fetch unsupported;
- PATH_BLIT_PIPE inert=1 true=1; PATH_BLIT_NONBBD nil/error; flag-off nil/error/no inert trace;
- TLS16 status4 and authored v4 status4.
IMPORTANT gate update: DELTA8 item4 makes true-MRT+fetch path_blit an inert PSO in backboardd, not a generic pipeline/status5 draw. With TEGU_INERT_PIPELINES on/backboardd expect inert1 and no draw job; flag-off/non-backboardd expect nil/error. Please replace the old TRUE_MRT status5 gate with the inert contract. Production hashes: encoder 5dd90110bf0fa51edfd43b2d32cffa68f8f2cbcdf652045df8b1c24d68a8996a, pipeline eb4eb03141c11e71315f5bfebd1043b009229185fe792683834d284da51631fb, submit 59ad68ab62d3235b5b95bf82261ff1393185309df4460d7ac507817475b5ff95. No native/phone/publish/commit.
